Z||000009||Nashco||11-18-2001||04:45 AM||||Actually, VW released that concept to the public a couple years ago.  They keep releasing different concepts, so it may not be too far-fetched.  They have been building some BAD mofos lately; the new Lamborghini Murcielago, that 249 mph luxury Bugatti, and this car....makes you wonder where the hell they're getting all this cash from!  Well, as we all know, VWs aren't that cheap, and you do see a lot of them out there <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I'm a big VW fan myself; I love german engineering, and VW are the starter rank for german cars.  I have an old bug (yeah...very weak in stock form...but they are easy to bring to life) that is a ton of fun.  I dunno about Hitler making any modifications to the original VW/Porsche cars though...Hitler wasn't much of an engineer compared to Ferdinand, he just gave the green light (made the order..whatever).<P>The W12 is a very impressive motor.  It's wide as hell, but still a VERY compact package.  The W18 is even more impressive...WOW...what a motor.  The new bugatti 249 mph concept uses the W motor.<P>Just a side note, am I the only one who thinks this VW W12 looks a LOT like the Diablo body style?  Remember, VW does own Lamborghini (through Audi), and they are using the VW symbol on this car.  Think they have plans to make an even more affordable super car than the Diablo?  Sure would be nice to see some real cars roll off the floor in large numbers like that one.  Perhaps VW is just trying to expose it's name/image but won't release this car because they know it would cut into their large profits made with Lamborghini.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
